Description: Slimmer CDJ/XDJ-style beatgrid overlay
 Restyles the rekordbox beatgrid markers introduced by xdj-hardware.patch to
 match the Pioneer CDJ/XDJ look, where the grid is drawn as short ticks at the
 top and bottom edges of the waveform rather than lines and arrows through the
 whole height.
 .
 1. Every-beat marks were full-height vertical lines; they are now short ticks
    at the top and bottom edges only (kBeatTickFraction of the waveform height).
    The software renderer keeps the top tick in m_beats and adds a bottom tick
    in a new m_beatsBottom vector; the allshader renderer keeps the top tick in
    m_vertices (so its reserved vertex count is unchanged) and adds the bottom
    tick in a new m_beatBottomVertices buffer drawn in the same colour.
 .
 2. Bar-start (downbeat) markers were large red triangles/arrows; they are now
    thin red vertical bars (kBarHalfWidth) at the top and bottom, the same
    height as the beat ticks. In the allshader renderer the two triangles per
    downbeat become two rectangles, so its downbeat reserve doubles to 12
    vertices per bar.
 .
 Size is controlled by two named constants in each renderer: kBeatTickFraction
 (tick/bar height, as a fraction of the waveform height) and kBarHalfWidth (red
 bar half-width in px). Applied after perf-render-repaint.patch, on top of its
 batched QPainterPath / reused-member draw path.
Author: Pioneered fork
Forwarded: no

